WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.718
Structured output turns generated text into a data contract.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:07.857
The lab expects a tool decision containing a name and string arguments,

00:00:07.857 --> 00:00:10.184
or a final decision containing an answer.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:15.353
JSON syntax alone is insufficient: a syntactically valid object may contain an

00:00:15.353 --> 00:00:20.371
unknown tool, a negative amount, a huge string, or an unauthorized account

00:00:20.371 --> 00:00:20.789
identifier.

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:22.186
Validate in layers.

00:00:22.336 --> 00:00:27.783
Parse the response, check its shape, verify allowed action types, constrain field

00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:31.415
lengths and ranges, and finally apply business authorization.

00:00:31.565 --> 00:00:34.882
Reject unknown or mismatched fields when they can change meaning.

00:00:35.032 --> 00:00:39.385
A retry for malformed output needs its own budget; an unlimited repair

00:00:39.385 --> 00:00:41.925
loop merely moves the runaway behavior elsewhere.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:45.739
OllamaModel requests JSON mode and parses the message content.

00:00:45.889 --> 00:00:48.475
Agent then rejects an unregistered shell tool.

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:53.525
SupportTools additionally requires the argument set to contain exactly orderId for a

00:00:53.525 --> 00:00:53.934
lookup.

00:00:54.084 --> 00:00:58.449
Consequently JSON mode is a formatting aid while the Java validators define

00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:00.632
what the application can actually do.

00:01:00.782 --> 00:01:05.188
Add test inputs for a numeric orderId, a missing type, an unknown

00:01:05.188 --> 00:01:08.859
tool, an excessively large answer, and an extra tenant argument.

00:01:09.009 --> 00:01:11.862
Decide which validation layer should reject each.

00:01:12.012 --> 00:01:14.902
The adapter rejects non-string argument values.

00:01:15.052 --> 00:01:19.509
The engine rejects missing or unknown action types and oversized final answers.

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:21.970
The tool rejects the extra tenant field.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.100
Add a schema for exact top-level fields if you need strict compatibility

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.421
and version it before changing the contract.

00:01:28.571 --> 00:01:29.242
Question.

00:01:29.392 --> 00:01:32.321
Why validate after schema-constrained generation?

00:01:32.471 --> 00:01:33.047
Answer.

00:01:33.197 --> 00:01:38.199
Provider capabilities differ and schemas cannot encode every authorization or business rule.

00:01:38.349 --> 00:01:39.021
Question.

00:01:39.171 --> 00:01:43.105
Should malformed model JSON produce a successful user response?

00:01:43.255 --> 00:01:43.831
Answer.

00:01:43.981 --> 00:01:44.465
No.

00:01:44.615 --> 00:01:48.727
Return a controlled failure or a bounded retry, and record a parse

00:01:48.727 --> 00:01:49.754
or validation metric.
